  "responses": {
    "short": {
      "text": "Designing a reliable file backup system is not merely about copying data from one drive to another; it is about building a **resilience strategy**. A backup is only reliable if it can be restored quickly and accurately when a disaster occurs.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. The Foundation: The 3-2-1 Backup Rule\nBefore diving into technical details, adhere to the industry standard **3-2-1 Rule**:\n*   **3** copies of your data (the original and two backups).\n*   **2** different media types (e.g., an",
