    "long": {
      "text": "Designing a reliable file backup system requires a shift in mindset from \"backing up\" (the act of copying data) to \"restoring\" (the act of recovering data). A backup is only successful if the restoration process works.\n\nBelow is a comprehensive architectural guide to designing a professional-grade file backup system.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Backup Strategies: Full vs. Incremental\nA reliable system rarely relies on a single method; it uses a hybrid approach to balance storage efficiency with recovery speed.\n\n#### Full Backups\nA full backup copies all selected files and folders.\n*   **Pros:** Simplest to restore;",
